# USE flags for the sway (real hardware) flavour.
#
# One rootfs serves every arm64 board - gentoo-sway-pine64 reuses the sway
# rootfs and only swaps kernel and partition layout - so mesa carries the
# Gallium driver for each supported SoC. They coexist in one libgallium and
# the driver is selected at runtime from the DRM device the board exposes.
#
#   pine64     Allwinner A64,   Mali-400 MP2 (Utgard)  -> lima
#   rockpro64  Rockchip RK3399, Mali-T860 MP4 (Midgard) -> panfrost
#
# The matching kernel drivers are already in place: kernel-config-pine64 has
# CONFIG_DRM_LIMA and CONFIG_DRM_SUN4I, kernel-config-rockpro64 has
# CONFIG_DRM_PANFROST and CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP.
#
# VIDEO_CARDS is USE_EXPAND, so the flag on the package is video_cards_<name>.
# A bare "lima" is not a mesa USE flag - portage ignores it and mesa ends up
# swrast-only, which is what this file previously did.
media-libs/mesa video_cards_lima video_cards_panfrost
